on.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c6b"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c6b"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c6b","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.74 (A later skip after a selected block)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.74, p. 65, label record:257bm-c6b","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose the real half-greedy rule skips rank $c$, takes $c+1,\\ldots,c+t-1$, and skips $c+t$. If\n$$\n0<t\\le c-3,\\qquad c-2\\le2^{c-t-3},\n$$\nthen the precritical suffix bound at $c$ holds. It yields sharp capacity and hence an exact row at depth $2c-2$. The case $t=1$ includes Theorem 6.73; the proof also permits longer selected blocks. The arithmetic condition is precisely $t\\le c-3-\\lceil\\log_2(c-2)\\rceil$. Its role in the proof is to make the dyadic allowance $2^{c-t-3}$ cover the bound $|D|\\le c-2$ for the earlier selected support.*\n\n*To obtain cofinal exact rows by this result, the stated gap condition must hold at cofinally many skipped ranks $c$, not just at one rank or throughout a finite sample. A finite empirical skip frequency alone gives no such pointwise gap bound.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-c6b","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-c6b","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c6b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfGreedy_precriticalSuffix_lt_of_future_skip_after_takenBlock%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c6b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfGreedy_precriticalSuffix_lt_of_future_skip_after_takenBlock%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a9